 Why: A safe kernel crosses a worker boundary only after sema proves sendability, bounds, aliasing, captures, races, barriers, and control flow before lowering
 Fix: Use a read-only effect-free expression over checked Core compute operations, or move provider/raw code behind its typed `#Unsafe` boundary
